,title,link,text,language,family
0,Annobonese Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annobonese_Creole,"Annobonese Creole is a Portuguese creole known to its speakers as Fa d'Ambu or Fá d'Ambô (Portuguese: Fala de Ano-Bom, ""Annobón speech""). It is spoken on the Annobón and Bioko Islands off the coast of Equatorial Guinea, [2] mostly by people of mixed African, Portuguese and Spanish descent.",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
1,Creole music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creole_music,The term Creole music (French: musique créole) is used to refer to two distinct musical traditions: art songs adapted from 19th-century vernacular music; or the vernacular traditions of Louisiana Creole people which have persisted as 20th- and 21st-century la la and zydeco in addition to influencing Cajun music.,Fa d’Ambu,Creole
2,Ambu - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/channel/UCRdHz7r6eafvtFRyfwIZnNg,"Listen to music from Ambu on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
3,Ambu - Apple Music,https://music.apple.com/us/artist/ambu/1196729345,"May 20, 2026 · Listen to music by Ambu on Apple Music. Find top songs and albums by Ambu including Arte (feat. Ambu), Ponle Ritmo a la Vida and more.",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
4,Ambu music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCVFZjwdanZ1YHhjWt9TmmLA,Official YouTube Channel *AMBU MUSIC*,Fa d’Ambu,Creole
5,Annobonese Creole - Detailed Pedia,https://www.detailedpedia.com/wiki-Annobonese_Creole,"Annobonese Creole is a Portuguese creole known to its speakers as Fa d'Ambu or Fá d'Ambô (Portuguese: Fala de Ano-Bom). It is spoken on the Annobón and Bioko Islands off the coast of Equatorial Guinea, mostly by people of mixed African, Portuguese and Spanish descent. It is called annobonense or annobonés in Spanish.",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
6,Fa d’Ambu | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/fab/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..vLFRIDDHg6gsr71JcWrqq5h9K6ToUtpWLB6YDzVhi4M,Fa d’Ambu is a stable indigenous language of Equatorial Guinea. It is a Portuguese-based creole. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Fa d’Ambu,Creole
7,Fa d’Ambu - fab (Creole) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/fab/,"Fa d’Ambu – fab is in the Creole family, included in Creole, Portuguese based language class.People Groups who primarily speak Fa d’Ambu. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
8,The Story of Jesus - Fa D'ambu / Fá d'Ambô Language... - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2t_FB6putD4,"The Story of the Life and Times of Jesus Christ (Son of God).According to the Gospel of Luke.(Annobon & Bioko Islands, Equatorial Guinea, Africa) Fa D'ambu/F...",Fa d’Ambu,Creole
